-- title:
--   Uniformiser generates mathfrak m_{T,η} at generic points of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring in Mathlib's sense) and let $\varpi \in R$ be an element whose span is the maximal ideal of $R$, so $\varpi$ is a uniformiser. Let $T$ be a scheme and $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a smooth morphism of schemes, and let $\eta$ be a point of $T$ whose image under the underlying continuous map of $t$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, i.e. $\eta$ lies on the special fibre. Assume further that $\eta$ is generic on the special fibre in the pointwise sense: every $y \in T$ that specialises to $\eta$ and whose image under $t$ is again the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is equal to $\eta$. The conclusion is an equality of ideals in the stalk $\mathcal O_{T,\eta} =$ `T.presheaf.stalk η`, namely that its maximal ideal (as a local ring) is the principal ideal generated by the single element obtained from $\varpi$ by transporting it along the isomorphism $R \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R, \top)$, pulling back along $t$ on global sections to $\Gamma(T,\top)$, and taking the germ at $\eta$.
--
--   This is the statement that a smooth scheme over a discrete valuation ring has reduced special fibre at its generic points, expressed by saying that the pullback of a uniformiser of the base generates the maximal ideal of the local ring at such a point, so that it is a uniformiser of $\mathcal O_{T,\eta}$ as well. It is used in the analysis of Deligne–Rapoport style models of modular curves, where it feeds the results on integrality of germs of the $j$-function along points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Smooth_maximalIdeal_stalk_eq_span_of_forall_specializes.lean

